// Title: Outbound Network Connection Initiated By Cmstp.EXE
// Sigma ID: efafe0bf-4238-479e-af8f-797bd3490d2d
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-08-30 | Modified: 2024-05-31
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1218.003
// Description: Detects a network connection initiated by Cmstp.EXE Its uncommon for "cmstp.exe" to initiate an
//   outbound network connection. Investigate the source of such requests to determine if they are
//   malicious.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://web.archive.org/web/20190720093911/http://www.endurant.io/cmstp/detecting-cmstp-enabled-code-execution-and-uac-bypass-with-sysmon/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/network_connection/net_connection_win_cmstp_initiated_connection.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceNetworkEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\cmstp.exe" and (not((ipv4_is_in_range(RemoteIP, "127.0.0.0/8") or ipv4_is_in_range(RemoteIP, "10.0.0.0/8") or ipv4_is_in_range(RemoteIP, "172.16.0.0/12") or ipv4_is_in_range(RemoteIP, "192.168.0.0/16") or ipv4_is_in_range(RemoteIP, "169.254.0.0/16") or ipv4_is_in_range(RemoteIP, "::1/128") or ipv4_is_in_range(RemoteIP, "fe80::/10") or ipv4_is_in_range(RemoteIP, "fc00::/7"))))
